#
# What may cut in on the screen reader's speech (nightjar_rules.h NR1), in
# Eve: an alert (kind 1) or a change of focus (kind 2); page reading (kind
# 3) waits its turn. Eve holds the kind to the two that cut in, so a kind
# that is no kind (0 or below) is never read as one; KRON's half orders the
# kinds by urgency (below page reading cuts in) and answers it, and the two
# then disagree: held.
eve nightjar
cut_kind = 1 .. 2

cut_in {
  kind: cut_kind
}
